title: "pallet-revive: Expose the PVM code upload check"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Adds `check_pvm_code`, which runs the checks a PVM blob must pass on code upload and
      returns `Result<(), CodeRejection>`. It is not generic over the runtime, so tooling such
      as `resolc` can tell ahead of deployment whether a blob would be rejected. `CodeRejection`
      reports the measured value and the limit it exceeded, so tooling does not need to
      hard-code the limits, which may be raised in future releases.

      Code upload goes through the same check and returns the same dispatch errors as before.
      No migration is needed.
crates:
  - name: pallet-revive
    bump: minor
